==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɪtɚ/}}
* {{audio|En-au-titter.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪtə(r)|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
First attested in the 1610s. Perhaps imitative or perhaps related to {{cog|non|titra||shake, shiver, quiver}}, dialectal {{cog|sv|tittra||snicker}}, {{cog|enm|titten|t=to waver}}.<ref>{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref><ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

====Verb====
{{en-verb|titters|tittering|tittered}}

# To [[laugh]] or [[giggle]] in a somewhat [[subdue]]d or restrained way, as from nervousness or poorly-suppressed amusement.
#* Longfellow
#*: A group of '''tittering''' pages ran before.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[teeter]]; to [[seesaw]].

=====Synonyms=====
* [[snicker]]; ''see also'' [[Thesaurus:laugh]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|en|tittersome}}

